---
// Emergency Tower's privacy policy: the Privacy Policy URL for the App Store listing. Mirrors PastePerfect's.
// It describes only what the app does. Keep it in step with the app if that changes.
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const EMAIL = 'njvanderbyl@gmail.com';
---

<Base
  title="Privacy policy · Emergency Tower"
  description="Emergency Tower has no accounts and no servers of its own, collects no personal data and uses no analytics. How ads, purchases, Game Center and iCloud work."
  image="/og/emergency-tower.jpg"
  imageAlt="Emergency Tower: three patients are waiting, one lift, who rides first?"
>
  <article class="doc shell">
    <p class="doc__crumb t-annotation">Emergency Tower · Privacy</p>
    <h1 class="doc__title">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="doc__meta t-annotation">Effective 24 November 2026 · Applies to the Emergency Tower app for iOS</p>

    <div class="doc__panel">
      <p>
        <strong>The short version.</strong> Emergency Tower has no accounts and no servers of its own. Your game lives on your device and, if you
      choose, in your own iCloud. I don't collect personal data. Purchases go through Apple, and Game Center
      through your Apple account. If you watch a rewarded ad, the ad provider may process limited device data,
      described below.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who I am</h2>
    <p>
      Emergency Tower is published by Nathan VanderByl, an independent developer. Contact: <a
      href={`mailto:${EMAIL}?subject=Emergency%20Tower%20privacy`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>2. What the app does not do</h2>
    <p>
      I do not ask for or store your name, email address, location, contacts, photos, or any account
      credentials. The app contains no analytics SDKs, and it does not use the advertising identifier (IDFA)
      for tracking. The device name you set in iOS Settings is stored with your iCloud save so you can tell
      your devices apart; it never leaves your iCloud account.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Ads and consent</h2>
    <p>
      The app offers optional rewarded video ads ("watch an ad to earn a bonus"). An ad never plays unless you
      tap to start one. Ads are served by Google AdMob (Google LLC) and are non-personalised: the app does not
      ask for App Tracking Transparency permission, and it asks Google not to use your data for ad
      personalisation. To deliver and measure an ad, Google may process device information such as IP address,
      device model, operating system version and coarse location, under Google's Privacy Policy and its rules
      for how it uses data from ads. In the UK and EEA you will see Google's consent message (User Messaging
      Platform) before the first ad, and you can change your choice at any time from Shop, then Settings, then
      "Privacy options".
    </p>

    <h2>4. In-app purchases</h2>
    <p>
      Awards packs and the HQ Pass are sold through Apple's App Store. Apple handles payment and keeps the
      transaction record. I receive no payment details. Refunds are handled by Apple.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Game Center and iCloud</h2>
    <p>
      If you are signed in to Game Center, the app reports your achievements and posts your best scores to its
      leaderboards through Apple's Game Center, under your Game Center profile. If you are signed in to
      iCloud, the app keeps a copy of your save in your personal iCloud key-value storage, so your progress
      can follow you between your own devices and survive a reinstall. Both are part of your Apple account and
      covered by Apple's privacy terms; I cannot see either. Sign out of Game Center or iCloud in iOS Settings
      to stop them.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Stored on your device</h2>
    <p>
      Your tower, responders, currencies, settings and progress are saved in the app's private storage on your
      device. With your permission, the app also schedules local notifications (for example when a floor
      finishes building); these are made on your device and no data leaves it. Deleting the app deletes this
      data, apart from any copy in your iCloud.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Children</h2>
    <p>
      Emergency Tower is a general-audience game and is not directed at children under 13. I do not knowingly
      collect personal information from anyone, including children.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this address with a new effective date.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Questions</h2>
    <p>
      Because I hold no personal data about you, there is nothing for me to access, correct or delete on
      request: your data is on your device and in your iCloud, both under your control. If you have a question
      about this policy, email <a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}?subject=Emergency%20Tower%20privacy`}>{EMAIL}</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="doc__links t-annotation">Emergency Tower · <a href={`${base}emergency-tower/support/`}>Support</a></p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  :global(html) {
    scroll-snap-type: none !important;
  }

  :global(.site-header) {
    position: static !important;
  }

  .doc {
    --doc-accent: var(--color-foreground);
    padding-block: 56px 112px;
    max-width: calc(820px + 2 * var(--pad));
  }

  .doc__crumb {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 18px;
  }

  .doc__crumb a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .doc__crumb a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .doc__title {
    font-size: clamp(2.6rem, 8vw, 5rem);
    line-height: 0.95;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.04em;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }

  .doc__lede,
  .doc__meta {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 32px;
  }

  .doc__panel {
    padding: 20px 22px;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
    border: var(--border-hairline) solid var(--color-border);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--doc-accent);
    border-radius: 14px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(80% 120% at 100% 0%, color-mix(in srgb, var(--doc-accent) 12%, transparent), transparent 70%),
      var(--color-surface);
  }

  .doc__panel p {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .doc__links {
    margin-top: 48px;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 24px;
    line-height: 1.15;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    margin: 36px 0 10px;
  }

  article p {
    max-width: 66ch;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }

  .doc__panel p {
    margin: 0;
  }
</style>
